<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert de Sablé</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1150–1193</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert de Sablé was a French nobleman from Anjou and Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Knights Templar</a> from 1191 until his death in 1193. A commander of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a>'s fleet on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>, he became master after the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>. Under him the Templars bought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> from Richard for 100,000 bezants, but a revolt by the islanders soon led them to hand it back.</p></div>
